## 2026-10-06 â€” More CDP pitfalls (Furniture phase)
- `Runtime.evaluate` shares one global scope: top-level `const` from a previous call clashes ("already declared") â€” wrap every snippet in an IIFE
- A synthetic `pointerdown` still needs `Element.prototype.setPointerCapture = () => {}` (or `svg.setPointerCapture = () => {}`) patched before dispatch, else the handler throws
- A tool-button click and the canvas pointer events must be separate cdp-eval calls (React commit gap), or the pointerdown runs with the previous tool's handler

